nodes.body:
@LucasWilkinson thanks for the review. All six comments are addressed (replies inline), and the branch is rebased onto main `8530aed2b` to clear the merge conflict. The only conflict was the config registry: #61701 removed `mlp_speculator` and `medusa`.

- Merged your sajadn/vllm#2 as is (`DiffusionConfig.model_options`).
- `fix(nemotron): address review on config-driven AR mode and tests`:
  - reverted the warmup change;
  - `diffusion_per_request_temperature` on the HF config replaces the architecture check;
  - `NemotronLabsDiffusionConfig.canvas_length` is `None` in AR mode, so `ModelConfig.is_diffusion` is generic again;
  - removed the unused test field;
  - the GPU tests now run from the default Hub ID.

CUDA, October 14, 1x H100 80GB + 1x H200: the whole stack (#60287, #60288, #61734 and #61733 on top) passed all 111 tests in `tests/test_sampling_params.py` and `test_nemotron_dllm.py`, each in its own process. pre-commit, including mypy, passed.

@sajadn I pushed these to your branch (as on Oct 9); shout if you'd rather handle it differently.

AI assistance: Claude Code helped with these changes and the validation.

